Z||000013||c m west||03-24-2001||07:36 PM||||or just simply bolt ours in and drive - NO MODIFICATIONS - $175, all accessories included <IMG SRC="http://www.cwestco.com/Intake/Intake_gif/AirTube_500.jpg"> <P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000014||Slammed Fiero||03-24-2001||07:37 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=44673861&Sequence=0&res=high"> <BR>Lisa's cold air<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=44673863&Sequence=0&res=high"> <BR>My cold air system<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=44673866&Sequence=0&res=high"> <BR>poor little 5.0ltr... 75 mph and look how flat I am.... Damm...thats with the old setup too!<P>JM<P>I hate posting pictures...<P>How do I do it from photo point?? anyone?<P>JM<P>have a nice pic of me spanking a 5.0ltr on the track <P>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 03-24-2001).]<P>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 03-24-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 03-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||DXR_DAD||03-24-2001||07:50 PM||||Eric, I think the point was The Topic... for less than $100.00  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>Slammed. Get the location of the pic, from photopoint, copy/paste with [img] & [/img]<BR>the location between the [img]'s<P>DXR_DAD<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||fyerstarter||03-24-2001||11:02 PM||||Ha I love this place. Some pretty cool setups you guys got there. Where I am there are no fieros (least no done up ones) and people are always asking me "what the hell kind of car is that?". I love it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Anyway I'll take some pics tommorow of my car and my intake and post em here. As for using the stock intake tube I prefer a nice fat sparkly chrome tube to an ugly ol stock rubber one but that's just me. <P>I did notice a reduction in torque I forgot to mention that. But still I would rather have a higher reving free breathing engine than a torque monster, i dont plan on towing a boat with my fiero any time soon :P||||reg||1
Z||000017||Shiner||03-24-2001||11:27 PM||||I still don't understand how the stock V6 air intake assembly is *NOT* a cold-air style intake.  The air is coming through the vent in the side, and not the engine compartment.<P>------------------<BR>-Shiner-<BR>'84 Sport Coupe<BR>'87 GT<BR>'86 SE 2M6 (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000018||fyerstarter||03-24-2001||11:46 PM||||Well it is  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  But if you've ever looked at it there are lots of restrictions. Between the filter cannister setup and the water filter deal it's like a maze in there.||||reg||1
Z||000019||DXR_DAD||03-25-2001||12:42 PM||||So, here's the info I'm getting from all this.<P>1) Stock set up is cold air?<BR>2) Filter should be outside the engine bay?<BR>3) Straight tube less restrictions?<BR>4) Stock set up is not sucking hot air?<P>So, if the filter is inside, with a heat shield around it, ducted to a side scoop<BR>wouldn't that be the same as a set up with the filter outside? same as stock set up<BR>but with less restrictions? and less hassle<BR>changing the filter, cleaning the filter<P>That is what I was trying to accomplish with my set up,  Did I??<P>THANKS<BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||5
Z||000020||fyerstarter||03-25-2001||03:48 PM||||I guess the best way to put it is the easiest and shortest path for air to follow is a straight line. As you can see here the stock setup is far from that:<P>[img] <A HREF="http://www.fyerstarter.f2s.com/intake_diagram.jpg[/img]" TARGET=_blank>www.fyerstarter.f2s.com/intake_diagram.jpg[/img]</A> <P>As far as the filter location it doesn't really matter where the filter is placed as long as the the place where the air is drawn from is outside the engine compartment and the filter location doesn't interrupt the straight line of air-flow. It just happens that my filter is on the end of the tube so it is outside the car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> DxrDad your setup looks like it would work just as well and is a very clean looking installation too, much nicer than mine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000021||fyerstarter||03-25-2001||03:53 PM||||doh!<P>let's try this again:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fyerstarter.f2s.com/intake_diagram.jpg"> <P><BR>DxrDad I was wondering what is that short little chrome pipe on your intake off of?||||reg||1
